| T-US01-07 | Component/integration | Values entered in step 1 remain populated when returning from step 2. |
| T-US01-08 | Component | Verify loading, no-published-fields, invalid-configuration, request-failure, retry, data-preservation, no-stale-config, no-fallback, and non-disclosure states. |
| T-US01-09 | Integration | Add, remove, and reorder published fields for a country; after app reload or switching the URL to that country, verify the refreshed field set and order match the configuration without a frontend code change or redeployment. |
| T-US01-10 | Component/accessibility | Complete and validate the form by keyboard at mobile and desktop viewport sizes; verify keyboard access and an accessible label for each field. |
| T-US01-11 | Component | With no country in the app URL, verify the app displays the country selection screen. |
| T-US01-12 | Unit/integration | Verify configured field identifiers are unique and remain the same when a field's display label or order changes. |
| T-US01-13 | Component/integration | Verify canonical lowercase `co` and `cl` paths, optional uppercase normalization when supported, unsupported-code error and country-selection path, no silent default/redirect, and separation of quote data between countries. |
| T-US01-14 | Integration | Exercise configuration reconciliation for removed fields and identifiers, reordered fields, changed labels/help, new fields, changed validations/types, and removed select options. Verify compatible-value handling, full-form revalidation, invalid progression blocking, and removal of discarded values from active persisted quote data. Verify the summary projection excludes discarded values when US-03 supplies it. |
| T-US01-15 | Unit/component | Verify each documented value format and each validation operator using the architecture-approved type-compatibility matrix. Verify multiple rules are evaluated and one displayed error per field follows required-first then configured-order precedence. |
| T-US01-16 | Component | With one or more valid options, verify a required select starts on a non-selectable placeholder, remains invalid without a choice, shows the required error on blur/continue, and never auto-selects. With zero valid options, verify configuration failure under AC-US01-08. |

The complete multi-step quote and payment end-to-end test belongs to project-level verification after US-02 and US-03 exist. This story's relevant verification is limited to US-01 behavior and the step-1-to-step-2 return path.

## Proposed commands and project conventions

No runnable app or test commands can be specified from the current repository state because this is a pre-implementation specification. The developer and QA stages should record the actual focused test and build commands after an implementation is available.

Implementation must follow `AGENTS.md`: Angular 21+ standalone components, signals, built-in control flow, and no NgModules; Strapi 5+; typed dynamic form configuration with explicit runtime validation; accessible labels and keyboard operation; responsive mobile and desktop behavior; fictional data only. No Strapi write-privileged token may be exposed to the browser.

## Boundaries

- **Always:** Preserve US-01 traceability; limit fields to the active country; validate configuration at runtime; display configured validation errors; preserve entered values when returning from step 2; follow project accessibility and fictitious-data constraints.
- **Ask first:** Change this approved scope, introduce a new dependency, make consequential country/configuration/persistence decisions not resolved in the approved spec or ADR, or change the selected interpretation of age and vehicle-year boundaries.
- **Never:** Attribute human-provided clarifications to the original assessment; put a Strapi write token in the browser; use real personal or payment data.

